-- title:
--   Dimension $4$
-- statement:
--   **The rung $r=4$ of Challenge 7.** The sphere-packing constant of $\mathbb R^4$ equals its lattice-packing constant:
--
--   $$\Delta_4=\Delta_4^L .$$
--
--   The lattice constant is $\pi^2/16$, attained by $D_4$; whether a non-lattice packing is denser is open.
-- source:
--   Open; the densest lattice packing of $\mathbb R^4$ is $D_4$ (Korkine and Zolotarev, 1872), see J. H. Conway, N. J. A. Sloane, Sphere Packings, Lattices and Groups, 3rd ed., Chapter 1, Table 1.2, https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4757-6568-7

